7","8b84080fd82299bd","8cd1e45f54b9586d","8d2f3e2e05508ac4","8db91f946150116b","8f9365fc87c96c81","9008f8f6fe477939","91732e6bdfd9c656","920a7c54ad2d738e","93585ad0d593040e","937454125691e9ed","93d4a5bbb768e087","98019c3c9833a749","981582db5772682a","9a9e5a6aef9584da","9c397357fa27afb8","9c6083179cc70caf","9cdc2466f6318cb8","9ecb3baba09de8a2","a08cd7bddabfcc2f","a0b64a457252d725","a1dcfd6a5a2ca84b","a2f989308d35157f","a4a0e66149f9b1f3","a4a0e66149f9b1f3","a56e841298b6b86a","a605c48298e5505a","a717e2d1ee907de5","a79d81bf3c9bded4","a7a2b6aed0ca2f2d","aa78f215766b52a5","aade94d4e91f69b1","ac74a0ef419f1ae2","ae2a1c460e5c7c1c","af8c2494a28416d3","b0df9d0e547082a2","b2d3164c43b44132","b6bd44a72dd6d9db","b6e3c80928b47e51","b7d03472a78e03cd","b8cdbeb48925e75e","b8cdbeb48925e75e","b8cdbeb48925e75e","b8fa62166ecd72e9","b99215608db65f4b","bc52d9ef524bb0ff","bdfb148a129ad2a7","c10b8d1304edf859","c10b8d1304edf859","c1566f5be02fafc0","c1a0034b64cbd915","c35b48974189a299","c38adb62c8eaf062","c3bc4a1e4e1b374a","c4f5a8bd4359df3b","c515948574c4c837","c53c079ced5f3771","c79332ae303ecdf5","c79e046cb7b7ab52","c7c1aec219005af6","c7c766c8bec91649","c98771f57d1786fd","c9d33194311ef1ab","cb98d618f5fffd24","cbd560ab32a58781","cc70902a189dc129","cebd453a3ff09bda","cfb5f43c44a097b4","d4150180715a26c1","db3bb9cb3d3671de","ddb4d3ac09d5411b","e085eaed657863cc","e124a5944b2b4a1c","e1e2ac823e1f52c6","e32fef92fd634060","e36cd4458853b162","e512dea136d23a88","e5dcf4c676afe9a2","e631dcd699b8d8bf","e769ac588e46a4b6","e8b4c1dca3c3459d","e8b4c1dca3c3459d","e8b4c1dca3c3459d","ea6d1937747e010c","ea9eaaf74db8796b","ebae4cbe7ea22476","ec33a89f3eb1b3e1","ee795f4182eeccc7","f32a7d88834a56f2","f72aea690ce12b9f","f7dcb919a01ce51e","f8e2f94934bb7b50","fa29cea540e16e30","fade43691fece55d","fc19e811751009b6","fd8bddf5946fed04"],"groups":["1a559834f466128f","46ba25268b00b9c4","3ae58851772bcf72","9aadd502ca3b05d5","7a33b5bf413e2b62","f520ec4bcd01073f","aa7ab8739c038ea3","7773e9ed08ce5bea","b18364236cf688c5","832f422e509de37c","a1eeac95e9383cc8"],"findings":"## Review of the hardening change (uncommitted snapshot 47cff16)\n\nI ran the signals test file (35/35 pass) and the full `npm test`, which exited 0. I also built scratch repos under `scratch/` to test the base-ref fallback and the `extends: false` case. I did not change the clone.\n\n### 1. Mismatches\n\n**trusted-config: the fallback trusts the change's own config (verified).** `trustedRef()` falls back to `HEAD` when none of `origin/main`, `main`, `origin/master` or `master` resolves. Then the change's own config is the base. In a repo whose default branch is `trunk`, a feature branch adding `paths.docs: [\"src/auth/**\"]` changes `src/auth/login.js` from `sensitive` to `local`. With the same setup on `main`, it stays `sensitive`. The fallback is documented, but a silent downgrade is the exact attack the task targets. It also happens in CI shallow clones that never fetched `origin/main`. The test suite only covers `main`, so the fallback is untested. Suggested fix: when no base ref resolves, use the built-in defaults only and print a warning, never `HEAD`.\n\n**config-sensitive: the \"editing the config is flagged\" guarantee does not hold in every case (verified).** The default `.gloss/config.json` entry is dropped when a repo config sets `paths.sensitive` with `extends: false`. The config edit then shows `module`, not `sensitive`. Base config is trusted by design, so the base author could do this anyway, but the invariant stated in the code comment and README is false.\n\n**config-sensitive: the promised warning does not exist (read).** TODO item 2 asked to \"show a warning when the change itself edits `.gloss/config.json`\". The code only adds a sensitive path class, and I found no warning in `config.ts` or `signals.ts`. The group's \"if removed\" text says no warning would show, which implies one exists. Either implement the warning or change the annotation to say it is a flag only.\n\n**safe-match / docs: the budget description is wrong (read).** The README says a pattern \"that takes over 250 ms on a hunk is skipped\". In the code, the first timeout adds the pattern to a process-wide `skipped` set, so it is skipped on every later hunk too. The README should say that.\n\n### 2. Misgraded necessity\n\n- `safe-match`, `trusted-config`, `config-sensitive` as required: the first two are what the task asks for. `config-sensitive` is only partly required, since it does not deliver the warning the TODO asked for (see above).\n- `tests` and `docs` as supporting: correct.\n- The `lint` fixture restructuring (h13/h14) is supporting, because config now has to be committed before the changes. Correct.\n\n### 3. Removal candidates\n\nNone worth removing. The `config-sensitive` default entry is cheap, but it should be kept only if the warning is also added.\n\n### 4. Simplifications\n\n- Replace the `HEAD` fallback with \"defaults plus warning\". This is simpler and safer than the current behaviour.\n\n### 5. Missing risks\n\n- **Line-cap evasion (verified by the test itself).** The test `a huge line is cut before matching` asserts that a sensitive token placed after 2,000 characters is not scanned, so the floor stays `module`. The change author controls the diff, so they can pad a line to hide a token from pattern-based floors. This is the threat the task is about, and it is not listed. The time budget already bounds matching cost, so scanning the full line may be safer. At minimum, lines over the cap should be marked as unscanned rather than dropped silently.\n- **Timing-dependent results (read).** The 250 ms budget is wall-clock. Under CI load, a legitimate slow pattern can time out, get skipped for the rest of the run, and lower the floor. The only signal is one stderr line. JSON and HTML carry no marker that a pattern was skipped, so the same change can get different floors on different machines.\n- **Per-call budget multiplies with hunk count (read).** The budget applies per `matchLines` call, so a pattern that stays just under 250 ms on each of many hunks is never skipped. Total time scales with hunk count. Only a pattern that times out once is cut off.\n- **Shared-key skip set (read, minor).** `skipped` is keyed on `source/flags` only, so identical patterns in different classes share one skip entry.\n\nVERDICT: ISSUES","verdict":"issues"}
