de37c","a1eeac95e9383cc8"],"findings":"I found two problems, both **read** only. I did not get a test result. `npm test` ran past the 120 s limit, and `node --test test/signals.test.ts` was cut off at 110 s after printing only one benchmark line. Neither run reached a pass/fail summary.\n\n1. **Major (read): a change can hide a sensitive line by padding it past 2,000 characters.**\n   - Where: `src/safe-match.ts:19` (`t.slice(0, MAX_LINE)`), used from `src/signals.ts:~134`.\n   - Scenario: a change adds `<2,000+ chars of padding> password = leak()`, or puts a device write after a long expression or a minified blob. The `sensitive` and `contract` patterns only see the first 2,000 characters, so no hit is recorded. The floor stays low and under-rating checks don't fire.\n   - This reopens the evasion the change is meant to close, because the author of the change now controls the input to the cap. The new test \"a huge line is cut before matching\" asserts the miss, so it locks the behaviour in.\n   - Better options: scan the tail as well as the head, scan overlapping windows, or turn a truncated line into a warning or a hit of its own.\n\n2. **Minor (read): a slow-but-valid pattern is dropped for the rest of the run and lowers the floor.**\n   - Where: `src/safe-match.ts:15-27`.\n   - The 250 ms budget covers a whole hunk's lines for one pattern, not one line. On a very large hunk, or a loaded machine, a legitimate regex can pass 250 ms. It then goes into `skipped` and returns false for every later hunk as well.\n   - The only signal is one stderr warning, and `signals`, `hunks` and `show` carry on with a lower floor. The warning says \"catastrophic backtracking?\", which can mislead.\n   - A safer approach is to apply the budget per line, or to mark the result as degraded where the floor is shown.\n\nVERDICT: ISSUES\n\nThe full suite finished with one failure: `performance: signals over 800+ hunks finishes within a few seconds` (`test/signals.test.ts:583`). Analysis took 3,036 ms against the test's limit.\n\nI don't think this is a defect in the change.\n- **Contention:** that run overlapped with my second `node --test test/signals.test.ts` run, and the suite runs test files in parallel.\n- **Solo run:** the same benchmark printed `analyze of 900 hunks: 434ms` when it ran alone.\n- **Not retried:** I did not re-run the suite on a quiet machine, so I haven't confirmed the failure goes away.\n\nNo other tests failed, and the two findings in my report stand: the 2,000-character cap that a change can use to hide a sensitive line (**read**), and the per-run skipping of a slow but valid pattern (**read**).\n\nVERDICT: ISSUES","verdict":"issues"}
