for it.\n\n**2. Weak test (group `tests`) — verified by running**\n`padding a line cannot switch a trusted pattern off for the other hunks` passes because `b.js` really contains `foo bar baz`. It would also pass with the process-wide skip from finding 1. No test checks that an unrelated, non-matching hunk stays unhit after a timeout.\n\n**3. Misgraded necessity (group `config-sensitive`, labelled supporting) — read**\nThe group is not just a supporting rating. For a commit on the base branch, `merge-base(HEAD, origin/main)` is HEAD itself, so that commit's own config is read. A commit there can reclassify its own paths, and the only thing that stops it lowering its floor is the forced `sensitive` rating on `.gloss/config.json`. So it is required for the stated goal in that case. It is also the only delivered part of TODO item 2. Its `serves: trusted-config` link is therefore misleading. The test `mergeConfig does not mutate the built-in defaults` guards nothing this diff changes, since the spread already copies the array. It is a cheap removal candidate with no real impact.\n\n**4. Missing risk: silent fallback in `trustedRef` / `readRepoConfig` — read**\n`gitTry` turns every git failure into `null`. If `git show <ref>:.gloss/config.json` fails on an existing base ref, the code silently uses defaults with no warning. If `git merge-base` fails for any reason, the message wrongly says \"no base branch found\". Neither case is in the author's risk list.\n\n**5. Cost (low) — verified**\nEach `matchLines` call costs about 50 µs (20,000 calls on a 5-line batch took about 1.04 s). This is acceptable. The 800-hunk performance test still passes in about 0.6 s.\n\n**6. Simplification and style (low) — read**\n- `commitConfig` duplicates `config` in the test helper. Renaming `config` to the committing version would remove the duplicate.\n- In `safe-match.ts` the comment is unevenly wrapped: lines 6 and 9 run long and one line is about 190 characters.\n\n**Accurate as stated:** `safe-match` (required), `trusted-config` (required), the `docs` paragraph on base-branch reads, and the risk list (apart from finding 1's scope). I confirmed the base-branch read against the code, and the working-tree config is not read anywhere else in `src`.\n\nNothing in the clone was changed; all scratch files are under `scratch/`.\n\nVERDICT: ISSUES","verdict":"issues"}
